  "topics": [
    {
      "week": 34,
      "slug": "symmetry-breaking",
      "title": "Hidden turns",
      "idea": "Color a regular ring so no nonidentity rotation or reflection can hide its motion; optimize the number of kinds.",
      "gates": "K-1: align and compare a moved copy with a fixed original. Grades 2-3: organize small-ring tests and distinguish a construction from a minimum. Grades 4-5: explain obstructions and a construction for every larger ring.",
      "materials": "Three clearly distinguished counter kinds, unmarked ring mats and tracing sheets. Counter spots are about 28 mm wide; use shape or texture as well as color.",
      "pretest": "Test actual counter fit and a tracing-sheet reflection. Remove temporary home marks before comparing; reflected icon direction does not change a category.",
