    {
      "week": 35,
      "slug": "glide-borders",
      "title": "Footprint borders",
      "idea": "Build an endlessly repeated border with chosen motions and explain why doing a glide twice forces a slide.",
      "gates": "K-1: extend a repeat and compare every motif in a moved copy. Grades 2-3: compare shortest slides and glides. Grades 4-5: use composition to explain forced symmetries. Adults may read and measure.",
      "materials": "Exact asymmetric notched motifs in four orientations, long paper and tracing strips, pencils and rulers. Prepare pieces in advance; this packet is not a complete manipulative kit.",
      "pretest": "Check the four motif forms and reflected overlays on the actual pieces. A symmetric substitute can change the answers. Ignore strip ends and handling-card edges.",
