    {
      "week": 36,
      "slug": "nine-point-world",
      "title": "A nine-point world",
      "idea": "A two-attribute triple rule gives unique completion, a maximum line-free collection and a forced-length adding game.",
      "gates": "K-1 is conditional: first check both attributes independently, including near misses. Grades 2-3: hold both tests while organizing collections. Grades 4-5: unique completion, incidence counting and an all-cases maximum argument.",
      "materials": "Nine distinct large shape-and-fill tiles per set, selected mats and spare paper. Each combination occurs once; open, striped and solid must remain easy to distinguish.",
      "pretest": "The K-1 two-attribute readiness check is mandatory and unperformed. If it fails, use one-attribute preparation or defer; that preparation does not realize the nine-point result.",
