    {
      "week": 37,
      "slug": "mirror-twins",
      "title": "Mirror twins",
      "idea": "Rigid tetrahedral models distinguish a true copy from a mirror twin; repeated labels remove this particular obstruction.",
      "gates": "K-1: handle true rigid copies and compare all four labeled vertices. Grades 2-3: separate unsuccessful search from impossibility and reset each merge. Grades 4-5: preserve viewing direction, count rotations and explain two classes.",
      "materials": "Congruent rigid regular tetrahedral frames, fixed category labels and a demonstration pair. Safe preassembled frames with equal edges and firm joints are required; bendable arms can create false matches.",
      "pretest": "Mandatory actual-model pretest is unperformed: match a true copy, verify the intended mirror pair and viewing direction, then match repeated labels. Defer if suitable models or the test cannot be supplied.",
